LD_VTX_GPU_VERIFY=1 (diagnostic, default off): every GPU-fetch draw (KZ3 patch 2076, LD_VTX_GPU=1) is also decoded on the CPU,
once through the shared decode of rsx_vtx_gpu.h compiled as C over the exact block the walker uploads and once through the CPU
fetch, and the first draws whose floats differ are logged as [vtx-gpu-verify] (frame, ref, vertex id, base index, attribute
type/size/stride/offset/location, both values, stable range, spans, block size), with a count every 65,536 draws. For R&C ToD's
straight cyan lines with LD_VTX_GPU=1 (R&C pass 16): the host test (R&C port/rc/tests/run_vtx_gpu_test.sh) finds the
decode bit-exact for every format, so this checks the in-game element plumbing without a capture tool (those turn LD_VTX_GPU off).
Rebased onto v0.18.0 + KZ3 2c5081a5, 2026-11-02 (at the first v0.18.0 build): v0.18.0's rsx_vertex_fetch_many takes no
output stride (it writes at plan->layout.stride, and the plan is built from the same layout), so the stride argument is dropped.

